428	The strategies appearing in Lemma~\ref{lem:pauli-completeness} and in the conclusion of Theorem~\ref{thm:pauli} are phrased in terms of qudit Pauli measurements and maximally entangled states of $q$-dimensional qudits. For the intended application it is more convenient to work with qubits: since the field sizes $q$ used here are powers of $2$, the conclusions can be restated in terms of qubit EPR pairs and qubit Pauli measurements.
