321		$\{K_{e_i}\}_{i=1}^k$ (Definition~\ref{def:dual-self-dual-normal-basis});
322		the maps $\kappa$ and $\tr$ always refer to this basis. The \emph{binary
323		representation} of $a \in \F_{2^k}$ is the $k$-bit string
324		$\kappa(a) \in \F_2^k$, the \emph{$\F_2$-representation of $a$}; the two are
325		freely identified. Addition of representations is bitwise addition modulo
326		$2$, and multiplication is determined by the multiplication tables through
327		\begin{equation}\label{eq:eq-mult}
328			\kappa(ab) = \sum_{i=1}^k a_i\, \kappa(e_i b)
